<title>INDIA: TABLE-METAL, AUTO GET LION SHR OF INDIA LOANS-RBI.</title>
<headline>TABLE-METAL, AUTO GET LION SHR OF INDIA LOANS-RBI.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The metal, metal products and automobile industries accounted for the largest share of loan sanctions by term lending banks during 1996/97 (April-March), the Reserve Bank of India said in its RBI Bulletin for August.</p>
<p>	  Industry-wise cost of projects sanctioned by</p>
<p>	    term lending institutions during 1996/97</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Industry			 No. of	    Project cost</p>
<p>				  projects    Amount	 Percent</p>
<p>						  (Rs Mln)	 share</p>
<p>------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Metals &amp; Metal Products	121	 97,740	  17.2</p>
<p>Auto &amp; Auto-ancillaries	 76	 93,210	  16.4</p>
<p>Chemicals &amp; Petrochemicals   139	 76,300	  13.5</p>
<p>Textiles (other than Jute)   177	 44,570	   7.9</p>
<p>Electricity Gas &amp; Steam	 25	 39,820	   7.0</p>
<p>Electrical Equipment	    45	 27,470	   4.8</p>
<p>Transport Services		19	 23,510	   4.1</p>
<p>Cement				32	 22,350	   3.9</p>
<p>Pesticides &amp; Fertilizers	14	 18,350	   3.2</p>
<p>Telecom			     28	 17,890	   3.2</p>
<p>Pulp, Paper &amp; Paper Products  18	 17,140	   3.0</p>
<p>Pharmaceuticals &amp; Drugs	 67	 11,850	   2.1</p>
<p>Hotels &amp; Restaurants	    22	 10,250	   1.8</p>
<p>Non-Electrical Machinery	52	 10,100	   1.8</p>
<p>Food Products		     70	  9,000	   1.6</p>
<p>Electronics			 30	  8,730	   1.5</p>
<p>Sugar				 25	  7,820	   1.4</p>
<p>Minerals			     9	  5,300	   0.9</p>
<p>Rubber &amp; Rubber Products	16	  4,840	   0.9</p>
<p>Glass &amp; Ceramics		  23	  3,770	   0.7</p>
<p>Information Technology	  18	  2,550	   0.4</p>
